<id/20/2039/#concept> a <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E55_Type>, skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Whiting"@en ;
    skos:broader <id/grp/grp_customs_residuals/#concept> ;
    skos:definition "ground chalk washed in alum-water, to cleanse it from sand and other impurities, and dried in lumps; it is used as a polishing material, and for making putty and white-wash. A small delicate sea-fish, the *Mertangus vulgaris*. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 424]"@en ;
